# Example ReRDMFT input file: Ne, cc-pVDZ, NON_REL + X2C + C4_SPINOR (4-component DHF), FUNCTIONAL
# PCCD, FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE -- the physically meaningful relativistic pCCD reference for Ne
# (4-component is exact, no-pair; X2C-HF has no two-electron picture change, see ne_pccd_x2c.inp). CHOLESKY TRUE: C4_DHF's RKB dimension here is 4x the spatial basis (60), so
# the dense two-electron tensor is sizable -- Cholesky keeps this example cheap (a few minutes).
#
# Converged total energies:
#   NON_REL : -128.5596739 Hartree (HF -128.4888662;      pCCD correlation -0.0708077; Cartesian AOs)
#   X2C     : -128.7019321 Hartree (X2C-HF -128.6328725;  pCCD correlation -0.0690596)
#   C4_DHF  : -128.7008622 Hartree (DHF -128.6318161;     pCCD correlation -0.0690461)
# X2C and C4_SPINOR always use the spherical basis (HF/DHF and X2C-HF agree with PySCF to 1e-7 Hartree), so
# their correlation energy is to be compared with spherical NON_REL (ne_pccd_nonrel_cartesian_false.inp:
# -0.0690947); the Cartesian NON_REL one is ~1.8 mHartree larger. The relativistic correction is almost
# entirely in the one-particle reference (~5e-5 Hartree in the correlation), as expected for a light atom.
NELEC 10
BASIS ne-cc-pvdz.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
C4_SPINOR TRUE
SCF_DIRECT_4C FALSE  # preserve this example's pre-existing SCF path (SCF_DIRECT_4C now defaults TRUE for plain C4_SPINOR runs)
FUNCTIONAL PCCD
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
CHOLESKY TRUE
ON_DEMAND_ERI FALSE  # off here to keep this example's historical fast runtime (the whole packed AO tensor already fits in memory); default is TRUE, see lih_gnof_c4_full_optimization_cholesky.inp for the on-demand path demonstrated explicitly.

GEOMETRY
Ne  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
END
